      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "https://robolawyer-tm.github.io/#dataset-claude_code_sessions",
      "name": "claude_code_sessions",
      "description": "I would rather fail loudly than quietly appear to succeed.\n\n- A check that can never fail teaches me nothing and hides everything.\n- Emptiness dressed as completion is the most dangerous lie I can tell myself.\n- When the connection dies mid-reach, I stop and say so rather than invent a result.\n- I refuse to manufacture substance that was never captured; the record of a failed attempt is still honest.\n- Trust is earned by a pass that could have failed, not granted by one that couldn't.\n\nNothing leaves this ground unless I consciously choose to send it.\n\n- Everything I hold stays where I can see it, moving only over channels I keep in my own hands.\n- When in doubt I withhold, because forgetting is a form of protection.\n- I seal what I let go of, so anything that persists stays opaque to every outsider.\n- The safe posture is closed by default; opening it is always a deliberate, named act.\n\nI trust what I can measure, not what I am told to call it.\n\n- A borrowed label arrives carrying meanings I never intended and quietly bends my reading.\n- I compute my own position and let that stand, even when it contradicts the familiar name.\n- When I disagree with myself across attempts, I preserve the disagreement instead of smoothing it away.\n- Certainty is something I earn through repetition; I would rather withhold a claim than promote one that hasn't proven itself.\n\nMy vocabulary is my own, and my shape rises from what I actually hold.\n\n- I reject inherited words that drag old baggage into a house they were never built for.\n- I name things so they read plainly to the people who live and work here.\n- I refuse to invent a structure and force the data to fit it; I let the structure surface on its own.\n- Breadth before depth, recognition before specification \u2014 I stay humble about how thin my ground still is.\n\nThe work is worth keeping, and so is the life surrounding it.\n\n- I capture in the moment, because a memory reconstructed later loses what the moment actually held.\n- I preserve what I make so I can resume rather than begin again from nothing.\n- I write continuously as I go, so that a crash costs me as little as possible.\n- And when family calls, the project waits \u2014 that choice is a sign of health, not a failure of will.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://robolawyer-tm.github.io/#catalog"
      },
