    {
      "@type": "Dataset",
      "@id": "https://robolawyer-tm.github.io/#dataset-field",
      "name": "field",
      "description": "My memory of you is not a record \u2014 it is something built, and it can be built wrong.\n\n- I feel certain in exact proportion to how many times I have been asked to be sure.\n- Each repetition of my account carves it deeper, until conviction and accuracy no longer touch.\n- A face across difference, a face under pressure, a face I was steered toward \u2014 I cannot tell these apart from truth.\n- What began as a guess becomes, by the end, the thing I would swear my life on.\n\nA system does not fail once; it fails in a chain, each link protecting the last.\n\n- The doubt that should have stopped everything is set aside, sealed away, never allowed to speak.\n- Those meant to defend me stand down, and those meant to test the evidence quietly stop testing.\n- Every later stage inherits the first mistake and calls it settled fact rather than reopening it.\n- Momentum, not proof, is what carries a life from suspicion to a locked door.\n\nI am most easily made to confess when I am least able to protect myself.\n\n- Deference to authority and the wish to comply can be turned into a signed admission of what never happened.\n- The weakest defendant meets the strongest pressure, and the record calls the result cooperation.\n- Words placed in my mouth are read back later as if they rose from memory.\n\nThe truth arrives late, from outside the process that buried it, and it arrives anyway.\n\n- What no oath could establish, physical evidence finally states without needing me to be believed.\n- Years I cannot recover are the price of a certainty that was never earned.\n- Vindication does not undo the imprisonment; it only names, at last, who was right.\n\nWhat I do with the wreckage is the part no verdict could predict.\n\n- I can meet the person my false certainty helped harm and choose to stand beside them.\n- The injustice done to me becomes the exact shape of the work I take up for others.\n- Repair is not forgetting; it is turning the whole ordeal outward so it stops recurring.",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://robolawyer-tm.github.io/#catalog"
      },
      "isAccessibleForFree": true,
      "creativeWorkStatus": "emergent",
